{"type":"message","id":"177582da","parentId":"392c2b53","timestamp":"2026-05-25T09:34:41.715Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"exec_ts_ZTI0ODMwYTctNWNkNi00MmZlLTk5OGItZWU1MzllNzJiOWMz","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-run-20260525-072854/media/feature.jpg)\n\nMETA\n- SEO Title: Ethereum Foundation Strategic Shift: Vitalik Signals Pivot | Coinography\n- Meta Description: Vitalik Buterin confirms a major Ethereum Foundation strategic shift, with reduced ETH sales and a narrower mission amid researcher backlash and calls for new leadership.\n- URL Slug: ethereum-foundation-strategic-shift-vitalik-pivot\n- Categories: Latest News, Analysis\n- Primary Keyword: Ethereum Foundation strategic shift\n- Secondary Keywords: Vitalik Buterin, ETH price, Dankrad Feist, Ethereum ecosystem\n\n---\n\n# Ethereum Foundation Strategic Shift Confirmed by Buterin Amid Backlash\n\nEthereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin has confirmed a significant **Ethereum Foundation strategic shift**, signaling the organization will reduce its influence, sell less ETH, and narrow its mission. The move comes as the Foundation faces pointed criticism over its perceived lack of focus on ETH's economic performance, with the token trading around $1,100.\n\nButerin described the transition as a move for the Foundation to become one node within a larger ecosystem, rather than its central command, acknowledging community criticism played a role. This pivot follows internal turmoil, including high-profile resignations, as the tension between the Foundation's long-term vision and the market's immediate demands reaches a critical point.\n\n## Buterin Confirms Major Ethereum Foundation Strategic Shift\n\nVitalik Buterin detailed the Foundation’s evolving role as a necessary step toward greater decentralization. He stated the organization is deliberately shrinking its footprint to allow other ecosystem players to step up. A key part of this change involves the Foundation holding and selling less of its ETH reserves to increase its operational longevity for a more focused set of goals.\n\nThe announcement follows sustained pressure from critics who argued the Foundation’s actions did not align with its decentralized principles. [Buterin stated that the organization is choosing to use its remaining resources to pursue “longevity over breadth,”](https://beincrypto.com/vitalik-buterin-ethereum-foundation-power-cut/) a clear signal of its new focus. The transition, led by president Aya Miyaguchi, should stabilize over the coming months as the board expands to dilute any single member's influence, including Buterin's.\n\n### Foundation Reduces ETH Sales and Central Role\n\nThe new strategy includes a reduction in ETH sales. This ensures the Foundation can support its core mission for years without being entirely dependent on market cycles. The EF currently holds approximately 0.16% of the total ether supply, far less than the 10% to 50% often held by foundations of rival Layer 1 networks.\n\nBy stepping back from a central coordinating role, the EF expects other groups to fill the void, particularly in areas like marketing and direct support for ETH as an asset. Buterin, who holds nearly 90% of his net worth in ETH, clarified that these activities fall outside the Foundation’s new, narrower mandate. This withdrawal is intended to foster a more resilient and distributed ecosystem."}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":23,"aggregated":"![Feature Image](/tmp/crypto-run-20260525-072854/media/feature.jpg)\n\nMETA\n- SEO Title: Ethereum Foundation Strategic Shift: Vitalik Signals Pivot | Coinography\n- Meta Description: Vitalik Buterin confirms a major Ethereum Foundation strategic shift, with reduced ETH sales and a narrower mission amid researcher backlash and calls for new leadership.\n- URL Slug: ethereum-foundation-strategic-shift-vitalik-pivot\n- Categories: Latest News, Analysis\n- Primary Keyword: Ethereum Foundation strategic shift\n- Secondary Keywords: Vitalik Buterin, ETH price, Dankrad Feist, Ethereum ecosystem\n\n---\n\n# Ethereum Foundation Strategic Shift Confirmed by Buterin Amid Backlash\n\nEthereum co-founder Vitalik Buterin has confirmed a significant **Ethereum Foundation strategic shift**, signaling the organization will reduce its influence, sell less ETH, and narrow its mission. The move comes as the Foundation faces pointed criticism over its perceived lack of focus on ETH's economic performance, with the token trading around $1,100.\n\nButerin described the transition as a move for the Foundation to become one node within a larger ecosystem, rather than its central command, acknowledging community criticism played a role. This pivot follows internal turmoil, including high-profile resignations, as the tension between the Foundation's long-term vision and the market's immediate demands reaches a critical point.\n\n## Buterin Confirms Major Ethereum Foundation Strategic Shift\n\nVitalik Buterin detailed the Foundation’s evolving role as a necessary step toward greater decentralization. He stated the organization is deliberately shrinking its footprint to allow other ecosystem players to step up. A key part of this change involves the Foundation holding and selling less of its ETH reserves to increase its operational longevity for a more focused set of goals.\n\nThe announcement follows sustained pressure from critics who argued the Foundation’s actions did not align with its decentralized principles. [Buterin stated that the organization is choosing to use its remaining resources to pursue “longevity over breadth,”](https://beincrypto.com/vitalik-buterin-ethereum-foundation-power-cut/) a clear signal of its new focus. The transition, led by president Aya Miyaguchi, should stabilize over the coming months as the board expands to dilute any single member's influence, including Buterin's.\n\n### Foundation Reduces ETH Sales and Central Role\n\nThe new strategy includes a reduction in ETH sales. This ensures the Foundation can support its core mission for years without being entirely dependent on market cycles. The EF currently holds approximately 0.16% of the total ether supply, far less than the 10% to 50% often held by foundations of rival Layer 1 networks.\n\nBy stepping back from a central coordinating role, the EF expects other groups to fill the void, particularly in areas like marketing and direct support for ETH as an asset. Buterin, who holds nearly 90% of his net worth in ETH, clarified that these activities fall outside the Foundation’s new, narrower mandate. This withdrawal is intended to foster a more resilient and distributed ecosystem.","cwd":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-orchestrator"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1779701681715}}
